      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought we discussed that incfs files already have a Merkle tree, and they verify the data against that Merkle tree by default (like the signature-less fs-verity support).  So this ioctl really just needs to verify that the Merkle tree parameters match, then verify and persist the signature.  Aren\u0027t a lot of these checks unnecessary, then?  For example, deny_write_access() makes no sense, because no one should have write access to a file that\u0027s already being verified via a Merkle tree.  If they can, that\u0027s a bug.",
